    {
      "key": {
        "uuid": "5a890539_265b6388",
        "filename": "keystone/resource/backends/sql.py",
        "patchSetId": 22
      },
      "lineNbr": 269,
      "author": {
        "id": 2903
      },
      "writtenOn": "2014-11-21T05:04:56Z",
      "side": 1,
      "message": "So, the more I am thinking about this the more that I am concerned that the RoleAsssignment backend is going to be overly complex (for a custom one) to handle Role -\u003e Actor,Resource mappings.\n\nThis works well for a SQL-system, but in the case of an ABAC type system (as role assignment), you\u0027re now needing to support a grouping of Action,Resource(project|domain) that resolves to a Role and then map that role to the Resource(role) that everything expects to be able to act on.\n\nThis feels like it\u0027s going to be a really bad UX.\n\nI need some clarification on how Role being (even as you said in a previous comment) the lingua franca makes the assignment backend better / easier to develop for vs. letting the assignment backend control the resulting Role as well. Alternatively, the Assignment backend may ignore the role(s) and produce something else, which in itself has some level of dissonance.",
      "revId": "8ae1364fd804b80972a8191e0b021a09610180dd",
      "serverId": "4a232e18-c5a9-48ee-94c0-e04e7cca6543",
      "unresolved": false
    },
    {
      "key": {
        "uuid": "5a890539_4caca9ed",
        "filename": "keystone/resource/backends/sql.py",
        "patchSetId": 22
      },
      "lineNbr": 269,
      "author": {
        "id": 5707
      },
      "writtenOn": "2014-11-25T14:41:23Z",
      "side": 1,
      "message": "So these are all valid questions...and I have posted some information to the dev mailing list (see: http://lists.openstack.org/pipermail/openstack-dev/2014-November/051481.html).\n\nI guess at some level we have to decide which concepts are \"global\" and which are part of \"multi-tenant\" support in its broadest terms.  E.g.  Do we want individual domains to be able to build abstractions that are meaningful to them? (yes).  Do we want flexibility to support different assignments models? (yes). However, we might consider \"base roles\" are really on a trajectory to become \"the list of capabilities of supported services\", to which we will want to provide support for access control.  If roles really become service capabilities, then it doesn\u0027t feel to me that they should be (effectively) definable by anything that is \"multi tenant pluggable\"...they are system-wide (or, perhaps more correctly, service-wide).",
      "parentUuid": "5a890539_265b6388",
      "revId": "8ae1364fd804b80972a8191e0b021a09610180dd",
      "serverId": "4a232e18-c5a9-48ee-94c0-e04e7cca6543",
      "unresolved": false
    },
